<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2014/Oak-Hill.jpg" alt="Plein air painting of a single tree in the middle of a field. The painting also features a distant treeline and cloudy sky." width="450" height="339" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Oak Hill Farm. 9x12, oil on linen panel. 2014.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I think this is one of my more adventurous plein paintings of the year: I had to work quickly to get the sky down before it changed too much and rearrange elements in the scene in front of me to make a good picture. All while I stood in a horse pasture where the flies created a cloud around my head as I painted.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I used the same palette as for my last five or six landscape paintings, but added viridian so that I could mix it with red and get a base gray to use for the sky.</p>